      <span class="tg-hero__type">Topical Study</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">The Faith Once Delivered</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        Every Christian has a confession. The only question is whether it is written
        down, held accountable, and open to correction by Scripture — or carried
        around unexamined. This study traces the confessing instinct from the creeds
        already embedded in the New Testament, through the early rule of faith and the
        ecumenical creeds, into the denominational confessions of the Reformation era
        and after. It maps the very large territory the traditions hold in common
        before it maps the genuine divisions, and it ends with tables setting out
        confessional belief tradition by tradition, with the documents and the texts
        each position rests on.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>Beloved, although I was very eager to write to you about our common salvation,
           I found it necessary to write appealing to you to contend for the faith that
           was once for all delivered to the saints.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Jude 3">Jude 3</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
