           ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

      <section class="tg-section" id="overlap">
        <h2 class="tg-section__heading">The Overlap — What Nearly Everyone Confesses</h2>

        <p>Denominational argument is loud, and it distorts the scale of things. Set
        the confessions side by side and the striking result is not how much they
        disagree but how much of the ground is shared and how early most of it was
        settled. The following is confessed, in substantially the same terms, by Roman
        Catholics, Eastern Orthodox, Lutherans, Reformed and Presbyterians, Anglicans,
        Methodists, and the great majority of Baptists and Pentecostals.</p>

        <table class="tg-compare">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Held in common</th>
              <th>Confessional anchor</th>
              <th>Scriptural anchor</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>One God in three persons</strong>, of one substance, equal in
              power and glory; not three gods, and not one person in three modes</td>
              <td>Nicene Creed; Athanasian Creed; reaffirmed in Augsburg I, Belgic 8–9,
              Thirty-Nine Articles I, Westminster 2.3, Second London 2.3, Articles of
              Religion I, AG Fundamental Truths 2</td>
              <td><a class="ref" data-ref="Deuteronomy 6:4">Deuteronomy 6:4</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="Matthew 28:19">Matthew 28:19</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="John 1:1">John 1:1</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="2 Corinthians 13:14">2 Corinthians 13:14</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Christ is true God and true man</strong>, one person in two
              natures, unconfused and undivided</td>
              <td>Chalcedonian Definition; Augsburg III; Belgic 19; Articles II;
              Westminster 8.2</td>
              <td><a class="ref" data-ref="John 1:14">John 1:14</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="Philippians 2:6-8">Philippians 2:6–8</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="Colossians 2:9">Colossians 2:9</a>;
              <a class="ref" data-ref="Hebrews 2:14-17">Hebrews 2:14–17</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Conceived by the Holy Spirit, born of the Virgin Mary</strong></td>
