              <th>Scripture appealed to</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Roman Catholic</strong></td>
              <td>Transubstantiation: the whole substance of bread and wine is changed
              into the body and blood, the appearances alone remaining. Lateran IV (1215)
              first uses the term dogmatically; Trent XIII ch. 4 and canon 2 define it;
